# A message that leaves the list leaves the reader at once (issue: a deleted message stayed in
# the reader for a second or two on a slower machine). The reader lays the next conversation out
# unseen and keeps the shown one meanwhile, but one whose message left stays at most 150 ms
# (reader::LEFT_SHOWN); then the next shows as far as it is laid out. Here the next message's
# layout can't finish: a large message's inline image waits for the fake engine's FetchPart,
# which isn't answered until later, so before this change the deleted message stayed the full
# 3 s (READY_TIMEOUT). Every message is fictional. Run:
#   tools/headless.sh 36 target/debug/sealwax --self-test tests/selftest/reader-leave.sealwax-test

desktop tiling
resize 1440 900
engine-attach
triage-mark-read-on-open false
mail-account Files
files-add-text cid
sleep 1100
files-add simple
assert-list-count 2

# The simple message is shown; deleting it selects the large one, whose image never comes in
# time: the deleted message is off the reader well within the 3 s a layout may take.
list-select 0
wait-until assert-files message simple
focus list
measure-leave numbersign 1 1000
assert-files message cid
engine-expect fetch-part
assert-files cid-loaded 0
engine-reply part-fetched ok
wait-until assert-files cid-loaded 1
